§ `Section 2015(p): obtaining cash by destroying food and collecting deposits`

-- src:887 | Subject to any requirements established by the Secretary, any person who has been found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b) to have intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount shall be ineligible for benefits under this chapter for such period of time as the Secretary shall prescribe by regulation.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(p) (src:887-887)
GIVEN `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(p) the person is ineligible for benefits` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who has been found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b) to have intentionally obtained cash by" the stated means; the text does not speak of anyone outside that class
    IF `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` AND `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:887 | Subject to any requirements established by the Secretary, any person who has been found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b) to have intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount shall be ineligible for benefits under this chapter for such period of time as the Secretary shall prescribe by regulation.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(p) (src:887-887)
GIVEN `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of ineligibility`
`s 2015(p) the period of ineligibility` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "for such period of time as the Secretary shall prescribe by regulation", so the answer is the core's value that says the period is not stated in this text, never a number; and "Subject to any requirements established by the Secretary"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a person outside the class of "any person who has been found ..." has no period under this subsection
    IF `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` AND `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount`
        THEN JUST `for a period the Secretary prescribes by regulation, not stated in this text`
        ELSE NOTHING

