§ `Section 2015(r): certain convicted felons`

-- What the person is convicted of. Clauses (i) to (iii) name offenses by the section or chapter that creates them; clause (iv) turns on a definition in another title; clause (v) turns on the Attorney General.
DECLARE `s 2015(r)(1)(A) offense` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(i) aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18`
    `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(ii) murder under section 1111 of title 18`
    `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(iii) an offense under chapter 110 of title 18`
    `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(iv) a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in section 13925(a) of title 42`
    `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(v) an offense under State law` HAS `the Attorney General has determined that it is substantially similar to an offense described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2015(r)(1)(A) some other offense`

-- src:893 | (A) the individual is convicted of—
-- src:894 | (i) aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18;
-- src:895 | (ii) murder under section 1111 of title 18;
-- src:896 | (iii) an offense under chapter 110 of title 18;
-- src:897 | (iv) a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in 13925(a) [Footnote: 3 So in original. Probably should be preceded by “section”.] of title 42; or
-- src:898 | (v) an offense under State law determined by the Attorney General to be substantially similar to an offense described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii); and
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(r)(1)(A) (src:893-898)
GIVEN offense IS A `s 2015(r)(1)(A) offense`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(r)(1)(A) the offense is one of those named in clauses (i) to (v)` MEANS
    CONSIDER offense
    WHEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(i) aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(ii) murder under section 1111 of title 18` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(iii) an offense under chapter 110 of title 18` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(iv) a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in section 13925(a) of title 42` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- the Attorney General's determination is the caller's input; JUST FALSE is a determination that the offense is not substantially similar, and NOTHING is none supplied
    WHEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(v) an offense under State law` determination THEN determination
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the individual is convicted of— (i) aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18; (ii) murder under section 1111 of title 18; (iii) an offense under chapter 110 of title 18; (iv) ...; or (v) ..." (reading (a): a failed "if"; the list is the whole of the condition)
    WHEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A) some other offense` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:892 | An individual shall not be eligible for benefits under this chapter if—
-- src:893 | (A) the individual is convicted of—
-- src:894 | (i) aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18;
-- src:895 | (ii) murder under section 1111 of title 18;
-- src:896 | (iii) an offense under chapter 110 of title 18;
-- src:897 | (iv) a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in 13925(a) [Footnote: 3 So in original. Probably should be preceded by “section”.] of title 42; or
-- src:898 | (v) an offense under State law determined by the Attorney General to be substantially similar to an offense described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii); and
-- src:899 | (B) the individual is not in compliance with the terms of the sentence of the individual or the restrictions under subsection (k).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(r)(1) (src:892-899)
GIVEN `the individual is convicted of an offense` IS A BOOLEAN
      offense IS A `s 2015(r)(1)(A) offense`
      `the individual is in compliance with the terms of the sentence of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(k)(1) the individual is ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(r)(1) the individual is ineligible for benefits` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual shall not be eligible for benefits under this chapter if— (A) the individual is convicted of— ...; and (B) the individual is not in compliance with the terms of the sentence of the individual or the restrictions under subsection (k)" (reading (a): a failed "if", clause by clause)
    -- (B) "is not in compliance with the terms of the sentence of the individual or the restrictions under subsection (k)": not in compliance with the restrictions of (k) is the answer of `s 2015(k)(1)` that (k) disqualifies the individual
    `s 2015 helper: both answers hold`
        (IF `the individual is convicted of an offense` THEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A) the offense is one of those named in clauses (i) to (v)` offense ELSE JUST FALSE)
        (`s 2015 helper: at least one answer holds` (JUST (NOT `the individual is in compliance with the terms of the sentence of the individual`)) `s 2015(k)(1) the individual is ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole`)

-- src:901 | The amount of benefits otherwise required to be provided to an eligible household under this chapter shall be determined by considering the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies not to be a member of the household, except that the income and resources of the individual shall be considered to be income and resources of the household.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(r)(2) (src:901-901)
GIVEN `paragraph (1) applies to the individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(r)(2) the individual is counted as a member of the household` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be determined by considering the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies not to be a member of the household"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies"; the text does not say how anyone else is counted
    IF `paragraph (1) applies to the individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:901 | The amount of benefits otherwise required to be provided to an eligible household under this chapter shall be determined by considering the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies not to be a member of the household, except that the income and resources of the individual shall be considered to be income and resources of the household.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(r)(2) (src:901-901)
GIVEN `the number of members of the household, counting the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies` IS A NUMBER
      `paragraph (1) applies to the individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2015(r)(2) the number of members of the household counted in determining the amount of benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies"; a household with no such individual is not addressed
        IF NOT (`paragraph (1) applies to the individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a household of no members cannot lose one
        IF `the number of members of the household, counting the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the number of members of the household, counting the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies` MINUS 1)

-- src:901 | The amount of benefits otherwise required to be provided to an eligible household under this chapter shall be determined by considering the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies not to be a member of the household, except that the income and resources of the individual shall be considered to be income and resources of the household.
