§ `Section 2015(s): substantial lottery or gambling winnings`

-- src:906 | Any household in which a member receives substantial lottery or gambling winnings, as determined by the Secretary, shall lose eligibility for benefits immediately upon receipt of the winnings.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(s)(1) (src:906-906)
GIVEN `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(s)(1) the household loses eligibility for benefits upon receipt of the winnings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any household in which a member receives substantial lottery or gambling winnings"; the text does not speak of other households
        IF NOT `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` THEN NOTHING
        -- the determination is "as determined by the Secretary": an input, and NOTHING is none supplied
        IF `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether winnings are "substantial" is for the Secretary
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:908 | A household described in paragraph (1) shall remain ineligible for participation until the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) of section 2014 of this title.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(s)(2) (src:908-908)
GIVEN `paragraph (1) applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2014 the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(s)(2) the household remains ineligible for participation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A household described in paragraph (1)"; the text does not speak of other households
        IF NOT (`paragraph (1) applies to the household` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall remain ineligible for participation until the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements"
        IF `s 2014 the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `s 2014 the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household meets the requirements of section 2014 is not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:906 | Any household in which a member receives substantial lottery or gambling winnings, as determined by the Secretary, shall lose eligibility for benefits immediately upon receipt of the winnings.
-- src:907 | (2) Duration of ineligibility
-- src:908 | A household described in paragraph (1) shall remain ineligible for participation until the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) of section 2014 of this title.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(s)(1) to (2) (src:906-908)
GIVEN `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date the winnings were received` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `s 2014 the household met the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) between the receipt and the date asked about` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(s) the household is ineligible on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2015(s)(1) the household loses eligibility for benefits upon receipt of the winnings` `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of eligibility "immediately upon receipt of the winnings" and after it, not before
        IF `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the date the winnings were received` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements"
        IF `s 2014 the household met the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) between the receipt and the date asked about` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `s 2014 the household met the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) between the receipt and the date asked about` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household has met the requirements of section 2014 is not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:910 | As determined by the Secretary, each State agency, to the maximum extent practicable, shall establish agreements with entities responsible for the regulation or sponsorship of gaming in the State to determine whether individuals participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program have received substantial lottery or gambling winnings.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(s)(3) (src:910-910)
GIVEN `it is practicable for the State agency to establish the agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(s)(3) the State agency is required to establish agreements with the entities responsible for the regulation or sponsorship of gaming in the State` MEANS
    -- fork F-s3: "As determined by the Secretary" is read as going to the manner and terms of the agreements, not as a condition of the duty; the other reading makes the duty arise only on the Secretary's determination
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the maximum extent practicable"
    IF `it is practicable for the State agency to establish the agreements` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
